Z||000005||hugh||06-26-2000||09:44 PM||||Thats really sick.Don't the people that run your government know what's important?Like at least a neutral color,or better yet no front plates.I think I would pay more for my registration if I could eliminate that ugly piece of tin on the front.I think I am going to run for president in November on the one plate platform and allow all the states only one plate.We would save so much money we can eliminate the national debt.  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Raydar||06-26-2000||10:20 PM||||GA has no front plates. The rear plates are white with black letters. Not too bad looking. <BR>We do, however, have smog tests. Anywhere that is within commuting distance of Atlanta. Very basic visual, and sniffer. They run the car on a roller (similar to a dyno) in order to  test it under load. No real restrictions on mods, as long as the basic smog stuff is in place. Guy that tested mine said that if I showed up with a V-8 Fiero, he would still pass it, as long as it passed the visual and sniffer. <BR>We have NO safety inspections. They don't care if the tie rod drops into the gutter, as long as the exhaust is clean. Of course, the really dangerous cars are usually gross polluters as well, so their numbers are declining.||||reg||1
Z||000007||olympic||06-27-2000||12:06 AM||||   Here in Saskatchewan, front plates are mandatory also.  But they recently eliminated the renewal stickers for the front plate to "reduce costs", like two 1 square inch pieces of paper were outrageously expensive.   Some other regulations include:<BR>1) no tinting of windows beside or in front of the driver.<BR>2) front bumpers must be within a certain height range.<BR>3)red/blue lights not allowed on the front of your car.<BR>4)you can still legally ride in the back of a pick up truck as long as you are sitting down.<BR>5)radar detectors are legal.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>6)your windshield cant have cracks in it.<BR>7)tires can't stick out of the wheel wells<BR>8)on most highways, the speed limit is 100km/h(62 mph).  You can usually drive 110 km/h without fear of getting a ticket. I wish it was 75-80 mph like in some states.<BR>9)our license and insurance system is pretty cool.  If you are a bad driver, the cost of renewing your drivers license goes up, not your car insurance.  So it doesn't cost you a fortune if you lend out your car to someone and they get tickets with it.<BR>10)hood scoops can only be a couple inches high.<BR>11)no smog checks(yet).  So you can modify your vehicle as you like.  We probably wont have any regulations for a long time since were twice the size of Texas and have less than 1 million people here.  Our biggest city is barely 200,000 people.<BR>12) by far the dumbest regulation deals with vehicle safties.  Any vehicle bought out of province must be saftied before being registered.  So I can buy my neighbors AMC Gremlin with 500,000 miles and no floor boards and register it w/o a safety.  But if I drive 45 minutes to Manitoba and buy a 2000  Chevy truck with 10,000 miles on it I have to pay the $100 to get it saftied.  Not very fair IMHO  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||TheFiero64||06-27-2000||11:16 AM||||Im from MA & I got pulled over 3 times because of the stupid plate rule  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> I finally got my plate installed. I hate this rule <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> ||||reg||8
Z||000009||Monkeyman||06-27-2000||01:38 PM||||Indiana--No E-check, no safety inspection, no front plate, no time change, etc.  Everyone needs to move over here. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000010||Gokart||06-27-2000||08:37 PM||||Hey TheFiero64, not only does it SUCK about the front license plate here in Mass but have you gotten a inspection done lately? Just got mine done and the freakin' sticker might as well take up the whole passenger side of the windsheild <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> To make matters worse ITS GREEN! Massachussetts SUCKS <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">||||reg||13
Z||000011||Carrolles||06-28-2000||07:41 AM||||In Alabama there are no front plates or inspections of any kind.<P>Mandatory Liability Insurance was just enacted on June 1.<P>Cars older than 1974 models do not have titles either.<P>You see a lot of junk on the back roads.  Independent Logging trucks are the worst.  When I worked in the country I'd go through about 4 windshields a year due to logging trucks.||||reg||1
Z||000012||stsmithgt||06-28-2000||08:42 AM||||I don't think my car ever had a front plate.  I hope "they" don't mess with me because I'll have to get another set.  Maybe the car looks sooo good without it, they don't bother me. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Some California cops aren't so bad.||||reg||12
Z||000013||Fformula88||06-28-2000||01:43 PM||||Two-Plate system here in New York.  To me, it seems normal.  Fiero's without front plates or brackets just look "naked" to me.  I don't see them very often.<P>There is a basic E-check.  They just look to see if all your emissions stuff is on the car.  No tail pipe sniffer.  I think NYC checks the tailpipe, but elsewhere in the state its just equipment.  <P>Also a full safety inspection.  Its a great way for repair shops to rip off their customers who don't know the condition of their cars.||||reg||1
