Z||000019||SibERThuG||06-30-2000||12:34 AM||||To any of you who don't already know this, a license plate is how a radar gun works. The plate is made of special metal which thr radar beam bounces off of and back to the cop car!! That is the reason for front plates.||||reg||1
Z||000020||Sillhouette.com||06-30-2000||12:48 AM||||Best way to get rid of radar beams is to punch a lot of little holes all over your licence plate.  Enough that when you look throught it it's see through but not enough to be visible by the cops sitting in their donut mobile.  Not too practical because most of us like to keep out hoods and cars shiny that is quite helpfull for the radar.  The other method is to get a scrambler that sends out laser beams all the time in front of the car so that the radar is confused.  <P>Later||||reg||1
Z||000021||olympic||06-30-2000||02:06 AM||||  Siberthug,<BR>Then how do they radar airplanes, motorcycles and baseball speeds at a ball game if a front plate is required??  Trust me, there is nothing that can stop the police from getting a speed reading on you except by using radar jamming equipment which is EXTREMELY ILLEGAL or by driving a stealth airplane.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Sillhouette.com,<BR>  Laser beams wont do squat to a radar gun.  Some companys claim they have products that will jam laser guns but it's highly unlikely.It isn't illegal  to use "laser jamming" equipment but I'm sure that if someone invents a successful laser jammer, it would be made illegal in short order. ||||reg||1
Z||000022||hugh||06-30-2000||06:38 AM||||Olympic is right,we have had trees clocked with radar at 80mph and they don't have front plates.||||reg||1
Z||000023||SibERThuG||07-01-2000||12:49 AM||||Must be different technology then, because my Uncle is a sergeant with the Massachusetts State Police and told me this is how it works. By the way, jamming equipment is not illegal because it can never be verified that you were using it; even if you have possession of such equipment in your vehicle. Police can never prove that you were using it!||||reg||13
Z||000024||Taijiguy||07-01-2000||06:45 AM||||Sounds like your uncle is jerkin your root. I'm thinkin if it were true, those of us who are always lookin for a way to keep from getting ticketed would have caught on long ago. As for laser, I actually read a story in Car and Driver once about that. They summed up by saying that one of the most effective measures against laser was to drive with your headlights on, that since laser is nothing more than concentrated light, that the light from your high beams could potentially interfere with the accuracy of the laser gun. Detectors are pretty ineffective because by the time it goes off, they've probably got you.<P>Taiji<BR>modified 85 GT||||reg||1
Z||000025||olympic||07-01-2000||05:12 PM||||   Actually, I think it's LASER that they aim at the license plate, not radar.  The plate provides a good reflecting surface for the laser beam.  Radar will bounce off almost anything.||||reg||1
